HEADIF:end of emulation file, start of m4 files;all
TEXT

Finally switch to the @code{m4exec} macro set.

The special chars for defining a set of characters is changed from "@code{[}" and "@code{]}"
to bytes with values 1 and 2. This avoids an issue when similar characters in @code{m4} are 
used to set quotes or comments. 

Extra input is inserted to be sure that all macros are recognised at the start and the end of the input file.
These macros do not generate output.
END
CODE
0_chars_pattern:0_l0_r-\@+*?~
0_atlast:++-+ 0_dnl
--+-
0_mset:m4exec
 0_dnl
END
